Z||000000||Fformula88||05-13-2001||11:39 AM||||I am going to have to buy some new rear tires for my Formula.  Currently, I have Dunlop D60 A2's all around.  I am very happy with their performance, but not happy at all with their lifespan.  The rears have only 13K miles on them, and they are down to the wear-bars in the middle.  I am not babying the car, but I don't do burn-puts either, and I'd expect to get more out of these tires.  Should I stick with these or try another tire?  ||||reg||1
Z||000001||TheFiero64||05-13-2001||03:53 PM||||I am verry happy with my Michelin Pilots. They give a great ride and grip and I have not noticed much wear yet in the 8 months I've had them.<P>Here is a rundown of them  <A HREF="http://www.tirerack.com/tires/michelin/mi_pilotxgth4.jsp" TARGET=_blank>http://www.tirerack.com/tires/michelin/mi_pilotxgth4.jsp</A> <P>------------------<BR>Josh<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://people.ne.mediaone.net/fiero64/Fiero642.jpg"> <BR><A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumList?u=1249362" TARGET=_blank>My pics</A>||||reg||1
Z||000002||yellowTee||05-13-2001||10:48 PM||||I ran cooper cobra on mine for 6 years (car is parked in the winter). They were sticky and I drove the car everyday.<P>------------------<BR>84 white 2m4<BR>88 yellow t-top, factory||||reg||1
Z||000003||RobertVol||05-13-2001||11:32 PM||||I know with all the Firestone crap on the Explorer's I will get it for this but honestly the Firestone Firehawks are great tires.<P>I have them on all four corners. These tires have nothing to do with the media frenzy on the SUV tires. The Firehawks have great grip and a good ride. Also, they keep good tread life. THey have QST which is like the aquatread crap, if you care. I dont, but some people do. Anyway because of all the SUV bad tires stuff You may get a good deal also.<P>||||reg||1
